# Build-context excludes for every image built from this repo.
#
# Added for the self-host path, where `docker compose -f
# docker-compose.selfhost.yml build` runs against a working checkout rather
# than a clean CI clone. Two things break without it, and both are silent:
#
#   - node_modules is ~1.5 GB and packages/*/node_modules are pnpm symlink
#     farms pointing into it. `COPY packages/client packages/client` in a
#     Dockerfile lands those dangling symlinks ON TOP of the node_modules the
#     image's own `pnpm install` just created, so the build fails with
#     missing modules that are plainly present on the host.
#   - packages/client/.next is another ~370 MB of cache from local `next
#     dev`, uploaded to the daemon on every build for nothing.
#
# Nothing here changes what the existing CI images contain. Every path below
# is either absent in a fresh clone (node_modules, .next, dist, out) or never
# copied by a Dockerfile — the images build these artifacts themselves.

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/out
# Must go with `**/dist` above, never without it. tsc writes its incremental
# build log beside the tsconfig rather than into outDir, so excluding only the
# outputs ships the host's claim that they are already up to date: `tsc` then
# emits a partial dist (an `index.d.ts.map` and no `index.d.ts`, no `.js` at
# all), and the next package in the chain fails with TS2307 "cannot find
# module '@starter/shared'" for a package that is plainly right there.
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.turbo
.pnpm-store

# Local secrets. Not needed by any image, and a copied layer keeps whatever it
# was given even when a later stage does not ship it.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.development
**/.env.production
**/.env.keys

# Native shells and their toolchain output.
ios
android
src-tauri/target

# Test and tooling artifacts.
playwright-report
test-results
coverage
.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# OS noise.
.DS_Store
**/*.log
